Aften: A/52 audio encoder by Justin Ruggles and Prakash Punnoor,
based on Fabrice Bellard's FFmpeg AC-3 encoder. Individual files retain
their original copyright and licensing notices. See COPYING.

Upstream repository: https://git.code.sf.net/p/aften/code
Vendored revision: ac1116da6a2b233f502bfb6ff87ac39692617459
Revision date: 2008-11-02

The surrounding internal/aften package provides streaming AC-3 encoding from
interleaved float64 PCM and one silent AC-3 frame from validated source-frame
metadata. It builds the single-precision encoder with one execution context,
using the upstream CPU-dispatched MMX/SSE/SSE2/SSE3 implementations on x86
and the scalar implementation elsewhere. Independent streams can encode
concurrently. A small state array preserves the historical per-worker padding
and bit-allocation counters without
using the original worker lifecycle.

Local source changes include these conditional adaptations:
- libaften/window.c and libaften/mdct.c, AFTEN_LEGACY_TABLE_PRECISION:
  retain extended intermediate precision when constructing the KBD window and
  transform tables, matching the historical x87 initialization arithmetic.
- libaften/a52enc.c, AFTEN_SAFE_COEFFICIENTS:
  reject nonfinite or out-of-range transform coefficients before exponent
  extraction can wrap and index outside its lookup table. Valid coefficients
  are unchanged. The bridge reports this failure instead of clipping PCM.
The source's original paths remain available when these macros are disabled.
- libaften/aften.h and libaften/mem.h: support static Windows linking and use
  the Windows aligned allocation pair without truncating 64-bit pointers.
- libaften/x86/gas_support.h: select 64-bit registers by architecture, including
  Windows LLP64, so CPU detection preserves the caller's complete RBX register.

This revision retains the original exponent-strategy search order. Later
upstream revisions changed that order and produce different silent frames.
For zero PCM input, the scalar build has been compared with the corresponding
historical encoder output at 32, 44.1 and 48 kHz. See package tests for the
supported regression fixtures. Streaming tests cover selected generated PCM,
channel layouts, bitrates and final-frame lengths; they do not establish
equivalence for every PCM input, platform or AC-3 header combination.

The C sources and build bridge are included so the linked library can be
modified and the executable rebuilt using the normal Go/Cgo build command.
